{"receipt_type": "instrument_sweep_finding", "ts": "2026-07-24T22:25:11", "finding": "silent-NaN class bug: a truncated/corrupt GGUF (a resumed curl that appended to an existing partial file produced 2834392928 bytes against the published 2784495456, sha256 c6c8c1e8... vs published 2d448a9a...) LOADS in llama.cpp and evaluates without raising, but every logit returns NaN. The NaN NLLs flowed through compute_signals into a calibration-style receipt that still reported measured=true, S=NaN, R=0.0 \u2014 a receipt claiming measurement where none occurred. Mitigation shipped in Gemma2FullNLLProvider.nll_tokens: non-finite NLLs are counted as instrument errors and degrade to measured=false, so the honesty invariant (measured means measured) holds even against corrupt weights. Discipline: verify GGUF sha256 against the published LFS oid before trusting any instrument receipt; never resume a partial GGUF with curl -C -.", "measured": {"corrupt_local_sha256": "c6c8c1e8f5cd3e719cbfb761c5d15662e81fe5c0dd2777c2db1e527bc994f5ab", "published_lfs_oid": "2d448a9aab894b8e8e18168cf3f490cb9f65632222f29f93514ac9ecc754debe", "corrupt_bytes": 2834392928, "published_bytes": 2784495456, "symptom_rows": "all five reference cases S=NaN R=0.0 measured=true"}, "scope": "gemma2-full-nll (llama.cpp); the certified Q4_K_M receipt is unaffected (its S values are finite and reproduce 3.19)"}
